contemper embeds two binaries it does not own the copyright to:

  internal/uki/stubs/linuxaa64.efi.stub
  internal/uki/stubs/linuxx64.efi.stub

These are the systemd-stub UEFI stub loaders, built and distributed by
the Debian Project as part of the systemd-boot-efi package
(https://packages.debian.org/source/trixie/systemd), version
257.13-1~deb13u1. Upstream project: https://github.com/systemd/systemd.

systemd-stub is part of systemd, licensed under the GNU Lesser General
Public License, version 2.1 or later (LGPL-2.1-or-later). The full
license text is in internal/uki/stubs/LICENSE.LGPL-2.1. The corresponding
source is the Debian source package linked above.

contemper links these binaries into a Unified Kernel Image at conversion
time by appending PE sections; it does not modify the stub's own code.
See hack/fetch-stubs.sh for how they were obtained, and
internal/uki/stubs/SHA256SUMS for their checksums.
